{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: five property notes, draft 2, at exact b4cb1893 (parent 21ce7204, base main 12cb8fa7). Artifacts 93b69a68, f41ed0fb, 3ef9ef28, f3fcb159, 66927f6b. This answers request a8e240f7, which replaces 9b4d7843.\n\nI read the whole diff from 21ce7204 and checked each source fact that the answers cite.\n\n- B1 fixed. Note 1, section 4 limits state properties to live states, with judge.ts:416 (`final` before guards) and validate/handlers.ts:263 (a comment has no guards). `always` refuses a final state, and a step 2 witness covers that refusal. The Lending example now uses `available-has-no-borrower`. A copy that fails `validateDefinition` (64 acts, 24 guards) is reported as not evaluated and never as a pass.\n- B2 fixed. The `intended` sentence is now true: `publish`, `borrow`, `return` and `cancel` send signer-supplied `content`. Note 4's send table lists all five sends, including `donate`, and matches examples/lending/definition.ts. Notes 3 and 5 print an answer as the publisher's word, never as a result.\n- B3 fixed. Both cited facts hold. application-package-v2.ts:80 reads the presentation with the closed list `only(value, \"assets,descriptions,entry,resources,semantic,v,views\")`. application-install-v2.ts:29 reads the `semantic` and `release` values by digest, and the proof reads no presentation part. Assets carry a path, a media type and bytes within the bounds (application-package-validation.ts:129 to 140). `ApplicationManifest` holds the `presentation` digest (application-types.ts:44), so the publisher's signature covers the asset. Section 7 states the K1 condition and puts the confirmation in step 2.\n- M1 fixed, and the extra point is correct: `compile` throws `CompileError` on any diagnostic (index.ts:706), so a warning severity is needed.\n- M2 to M5 fixed. The slot table, the `count` row, the kernel section 7 citation and the four form facts for one hold per tool and day are accurate.\n\nNon-blocking:\nN1. Note 4: \"anyone who has at most one held reservation\" describes the state before the act. After `reserve`, the signer can hold two. Say \"at most one other held reservation\" so the row cannot be read as a limit of one.\nN2. Note 5, section 3: a presentation asset is served in the release's screen origin. Say that `dap.properties.json` is then public to anyone who can load the screen. That is harmless for public claims, but the reader should know it.\n\nConclusions\n\nArchitecture: sound. The search uses the scope's own judges and fold, the authority table reads only forms, and properties stay out of the semantic digest and the install proof. The live-state limit is stated where it binds.\n\nSecurity: acceptable. No note adds an authority path, and no scope reads a property. Publisher answers are marked as unchecked text. The asset route changes nothing that platform code accepts at installation, and step 2 confirms this before any build.\n\nSimplification: acceptable. Note 3's first mechanism and note 4's first step stand alone and come first. The search waits on its measurement. Extending the existing `findings` replaces the new mechanism of draft 1. Nothing further should go.\n\nThe checks named in the request were not rerun. This review reads the text and the source.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:93b69a68849bdeefb76890bdcf51b78ff01c091a","binding":"assigned","head":"b4cb189335a80ae730ec8414f32c81f3f6dd1882","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f1441c29d85bb8f564136f27d16ce60bb29fe026\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:df3b7e9e5fa4f1782f6bafdd1c50dc8fee767745\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f1441c29d85bb8f564136f27d16ce60bb29fe026","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}